# Leave DATABASE_URL unset to run on PGlite (real Postgres in WASM, no container).
# Set it to use the docker-compose Postgres or Neon:
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://prepo:prepo@localhost:5432/prepo
#
# Put real values in apps/web/.env.local (git-ignored) rather than here. The
# `db:*` scripts read that file too. Check what is set, and whether it works:
#   pnpm --filter @prepo/web db:providers -- --live

# Where the embedded PGlite database keeps its files.
# PGLITE_DIR=.pglite

# This deployment's public origin. It is only used to print an absolute webhook
# address on the integrations page; nothing depends on it being set, and without
# it the page shows the path and says to prefix the origin yourself.
# APP_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Audio storage (milestone 4). Defaults live under apps/web/.storage, which is
# git-ignored. The local filesystem driver is the only one implemented; the
# interface is there so an object store can replace it later.
# AUDIO_STORAGE_DIR=.storage/audio
# AUDIO_STAGING_DIR=.storage/incoming

# Speech-to-text. With no key, recordings are still stored and the transcript
# upload/paste route works, but nothing is sent anywhere and the UI says so.
# DEEPGRAM_API_KEY=
# Optional, so cost is only recorded when you know your own rate:
# DEEPGRAM_COST_PER_MINUTE=

# Email for follow-ups (milestone 5). With no key, a message that needs email is
# attempted and then recorded as failed with that reason — never silently marked
# sent — while the in-app half of the same rung still reaches the notification
# centre. Set the key and the same code path delivers.
# RESEND_API_KEY=
# RESEND_FROM=Prepo <onboarding@resend.dev>

# Not built yet — push needs VAPID keys and an installed app with a subscription,
# and there is no service worker in this build, so no push row is ever queued.
# VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=
# VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=

# Extraction (milestone 7) needs a language model. It is reached through
# OpenRouter rather than a single vendor's SDK, so swapping models is an env
# change. Both values are required: with either missing, extraction is refused
# and the meeting page says which one is absent. The model is asked for a JSON
# Schema response and falls back to JSON mode if it does not support that; either
# way the reply has to pass the same Zod gate.
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# AI_MODEL_EXTRACT=nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b:free

# Linear two-way sync (milestone 6). A personal API key goes in raw; an OAuth
# token would need the `Bearer ` prefix. The token is encrypted with
# INTEGRATION_ENCRYPTION_KEY before it is stored, so without that key a
# connection cannot be saved at all:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64'))"
# LINEAR_API_KEY=
# INTEGRATION_ENCRYPTION_KEY=
# The secret Linear shows when you create the webhook, so deliveries can be
# verified. Set it from the integrations page, which encrypts it the same way.
# LINEAR_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# The desktop shell (milestone 8) is a separate app in apps/desktop. It reads this
# variable, not this file's database settings: it opens the web app rather than
# sharing a database with it. It defaults to http://localhost:3000, so there is
# nothing to set for local development. Any other origin must be http(s) with no
# credentials in it, and must also appear in the CSP's connect-src in
# apps/desktop/src-tauri/tauri.conf.json — `pnpm desktop:verify` fails if they
# disagree.
# PREPO_DESKTOP_URL=http://localhost:3000
